Schlesinger WH. (ed), Biogeochemistry. Elsevier-Pergamon, Oxford, United Kingdom.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Segarra KEA, Schubotz F, Samarkin V, Yoshinaga MY, Hinrichs K-U, Joye SB. 2015. High rates of anaerobic methane oxidation in freshwater wetlands reduce potential atmospheric methane emissions. Nat Commun 6:7477. doi: 10.1038/ncomms8477.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/ncomms8477</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">26123199</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Segarra KEA, Comerford C, Slaughter J, Joye SB. 2013. Impact of electron acceptor availability on the anaerobic oxidation of methane in coastal freshwater and brackish wetland sediments. Geochim Cosmochim Acta 115:15&#x2013;30. doi: 10.1016/j.gca.2013.03.029.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.gca.2013.03.029</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Martinez CM, Alvarez LH, Celis LB, Cervantes FJ. 2013. Humus-reducing microorganisms and their valuable contribution in environmental processes. Appl Microbiol Biotechnol 97:10293&#x2013;10308. doi: 10.1007/s00253-013-5350-7.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1007/s00253-013-5350-7</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">24220793</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Lehmann J, Kleber M. 2015. The contentious nature of soil organic matter. Nature 528:60&#x2013;68.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">26595271</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Blodau C, Deppe M. 2012. Humic acid addition lowers methane release in peats of the Mer Bleue bog, Canada. Soil Biol Biochem 52:96&#x2013;98. doi: 10.1016/j.soilbio.2012.04.023.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.soilbio.2012.04.023</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Miller KE, Lai CT, Friedman ES, Angenent LT, Lipson DA. 2015. Methane suppression by iron and humic acids in soils of the A